   "title": "Your Villages Weekend Recap: Brass on the Square",
   "date": "August 10, 2026 · By Susan Whitfield, Villages insider",
   "body": "<img src=\"post-2026-08-10-header.jpg\" alt=\"Illustrated sunset over the water with a bandstand, palm trees and string lights\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;margin:0 0 14px\">\n\n<p>Good Monday morning, friends. Pour the coffee, because we have some catching up to do. The squares were humming all three nights, a heron made the local paper, and one street over by Lake Sumter is quietly minting millionaires. Here's the scoop.</p>\n\n<h3>Brass on the boardwalk</h3>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/lake-sumter-landing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Lake Sumter Landing</a> had itself a weekend. Friday night The 789s got things rolling, five musicians from five corners of the country playing rock, disco and pop until ten. Saturday brought Bourbon Street Brass and those big New Orleans horns to the square. If you read last week's post, you know I pointed Gloria and her pickleball gentleman to that exact show for their first date. No word back yet. I am choosing to take that as a very good sign.</p>\n\n<p>Sunday, Pavani's Band closed out the weekend with a night of '70s and '80s hits by the water. A reminder for the newer folks: summer hours on the squares run 6 to 10 p.m. through September 30, so there's plenty of daylight left for dinner first and dancing second. The bar huts are also pouring their August special, the <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/bar-huts/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Berry Ripple</a>, raspberry and pineapple with vodka, 8 dollars for a single and 10.50 for a double. That one sounds like a front porch in a cup.</p>\n\n<h3>A million-dollar street</h3>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/08/08/home-in-bridgeport-at-lake-sumter-sells-for-1-1-million/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Villages-News reported Saturday</a> that a home in Bridgeport at Lake Sumter sold for 1.1 million dollars. By <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/08/09/another-home-on-same-street-in-the-villages-crosses-million-dollar-sales-mark-doubles-original-purchase-price/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sunday they were reporting</a> that another home on the very same street crossed the million-dollar mark, selling for double its original purchase price. Two in one weekend. My house has the same sunshine and better tomatoes, so I can only assume my number is coming.</p>\n\n<h3>The library that turned late fees into pencils</h3>\n\n<p>Here's a who-knew for you. The <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/08/09/lady-lake-library-donates-school-supplies-through-annual-fine-forgiveness-program/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Lady Lake Library donated school supplies through its annual fine forgiveness program</a>, per Villages-News on Sunday. Local kids head back to class with fresh supplies, and a few overdue consciences around here got wiped clean in the bargain. Everybody wins. If your grandkids are nearby, a library card is still the best free thing in town.</p>\n\n<h3>Small news, good news</h3>\n\n<p>The <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/08/09/collier-swimming-pool-will-be-getting-new-furniture/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Collier swimming pool is getting new furniture</a>, which I count as a genuine quality of life improvement for anyone who has ever fought over the last good lounger. And the weekend photo pages were showing off, with a <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/08/09/sunrise-view-near-ednas-on-the-green/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">sunrise near Ednas' on the Green</a> and a <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/08/08/great-blue-heron-catches-large-eel-along-hogeye-pathway/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">great blue heron wrestling down a large eel along the Hogeye Pathway</a>. That bird ate better than some of us this weekend, and I include myself.</p>\n\n<h3>Tonight, if you're up for it</h3>\n\n<p>Blonde Ambition plays <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/brownwood/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Brownwood</a> with their Top 40, Motown and everything-else show, and The Rundown Band brings '80s rock to <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/lake-sumter-landing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Lake Sumter Landing</a>, 6 to 10 as always. Monday is the new Saturday when you're retired.</p>\n\n<p>That's the weekend as it actually happened, no padding, no fluff. If you spotted something I missed, or you know which square band deserves a shout next week, send it my way. My little black book always has room for one more page.</p>\n\n<p>See you around the square,<br>Susan</p>\n\n<p><em>By Susan Whitfield, Villages insider</em></p>"
  },
