   "title": "Ask Susan: Which Square Wins for a First Date?",
   "date": "August 6, 2026 · By Susan Whitfield, Villages insider",
   "body": "<p>Well, friends, we're doing something a little different this week. The mailbag is open, and one of your neighbors got right to the good stuff:</p>\n\n<p><em>Gloria from the Village of Pennecamp asks: \"A very nice gentleman from my pickleball group finally worked up the nerve to ask me to dinner. It's my first date in &mdash; let's just say a while. Which square should we pick? I don't want anything too loud, but I don't want us sitting there in silence, either.\"</em></p>\n\n<p>Gloria, honey, first of all: good for you. Second of all, you've come to the right woman. The girls will tell you I have strong opinions on this subject, and I'm rarely wrong. Here's the scoop.</p>\n\n<h3>The golden rule of square dates</h3>\n\n<p>All summer long &mdash; June 1 through September 30 &mdash; the free nightly entertainment on the squares runs <strong>6 to 10 p.m.</strong> instead of the usual 5 to 9. That later start is a gift for a first date: dinner first, music second. You get a proper conversation over a meal while it's still quiet, and then the band gives you something to do when the small talk runs thin. Nobody has ever needed a backup plan while a live band is playing. Trust me on this one.</p>\n\n<h3>My pick: Lake Sumter Landing</h3>\n\n<p>For a first date, it's <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/lake-sumter-landing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Lake Sumter Landing</a>, and it isn't close. The water, the lights, the stroll along the boardwalk when you want a quieter moment away from the stage &mdash; no other square gives you an escape hatch that pretty. And this Saturday, August 8, the entertainment gods are on your side: <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/lake-sumter-landing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bourbon Street Brass</a> brings New Orleans brass and jazz to the square from 6 to 10. Romantic without trying too hard, lively without shouting over guitar solos. That's the sweet spot, Gloria.</p>\n\n<h3>The supporting cast</h3>\n\n<p>If your gentleman turns out to be a dancer, Saturday at <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/spanish-springs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spanish Springs</a> is The Fire Rhythms Band &mdash; Caribbean and Brazilian beats, funk, and Top 40, a full-blown dance party. First dates have been made on less. And if Saturday doesn't work, Sunday the 9th at <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/brownwood/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Brownwood</a> has September Dogs, a female-fronted four-piece with lovely layered vocals &mdash; a gentler landing if you'd rather ease into things.</p>\n\n<h3>One more trick up my sleeve</h3>\n\n<p>Get there before the band. The <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/bar-huts/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">bar huts</a> open at 4 with happy hour from 5 to 6, per <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/?p=307308\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Villages-News</a> &mdash; and August's special is the <strong>Berry Ripple</strong>, raspberry and pineapple with vodka, $8 for a single. Hand him one of those at golden hour by the water and let the evening do the rest. And Gloria? Wear the good earrings. He noticed you at pickleball; he'll notice those too.</p>\n\n<p>Got a question for me? Send it through the \"Ask Susan\" box over at <a href=\"https://thevillagesfood.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">thevillagesfood.com</a> &mdash; the mailbag is open, and no question is too small, too silly, or too spicy. See you on the square.</p>"
  },
