   "title": "Your Villages Weekend + What's New: Brass, Burgers & Soft Serve",
   "date": "July 23, 2026 · By Susan Whitfield, Villages insider",
   "body": "<p>Well, we made it to another Thursday, friends. The girls and I already have our Saturday mapped out, and I'm here to share the homework so you don't have to do it. Here's the scoop on the weekend ahead &mdash; plus a few changes around town you'll want to know about.</p>\n\n<p>One housekeeping note before we start: square music runs <strong>6 to 10 p.m.</strong> all summer, through September 30. Later start, cooler evening. I call that a win.</p>\n\n<h3>What to do this weekend</h3>\n\n<p><strong>Friday, July 24.</strong> Three squares, three very different nights. <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/spanish-springs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Penta</a>, a rock, blues, and funk band out of Daytona Beach, takes Spanish Springs. Over at Lake Sumter Landing, it's <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/lake-sumter-landing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bandemic</a> &mdash; forty-plus years of rock 'n' roll, from classic '80s to country-rock. And Brownwood is doing something different: <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/brownwood/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CLUB CTRL with DJ Lu-S</a>, a full-on DJ dance party under the lights. If the grandkids are visiting, take them to Brownwood. They'll be shocked you know what a DJ is.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Saturday, July 25.</strong> This is my pick of the weekend: <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/brownwood/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Swing Theory at Brownwood</a>. Seven pieces, big band sounds from the '20s, '30s, and '40s, plus jazz, blues, and Latin. Wear shoes you can actually dance in. Trust me on this one. Prefer classic rock? <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/lake-sumter-landing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Uncle Bob's Rock Shop</a> plays Lake Sumter Landing with a real concert feel. And Spanish Springs gets the <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/spanish-springs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Zee-R Band</a>, family-friendly hits from all eras, fronted by an artist originally from Brazil.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Sunday, July 26.</strong> End the weekend easy. <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/spanish-springs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bourbon Street Brass</a> brings New Orleans brass and jazz to Spanish Springs &mdash; get there early with a to-go dinner and a lawn chair. <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/lake-sumter-landing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sheila &amp; The Sound</a> covers everything from Aretha to Journey at Lake Sumter Landing, and <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/brownwood/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Dance Express</a> plays Motown and old school at Brownwood.</p>\n\n<p>Two quick dining notes. Eat before the music or grab something on the square &mdash; every one of these squares has plenty within walking distance of the stage. And the bar huts are pouring their July special, the <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/bar-huts/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Freedom Punch</a>, $8 for a single, while supplies last. It's red, white, and blue and it goes down easy on a hot night. You're welcome.</p>\n\n<h3>What's new around town</h3>\n\n<p><strong>The hottest line in town is for ice cream.</strong> The new <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/07/15/hottest-new-nightspot-in-the-villages-isnt-serving-booze/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Twistee Treat at Pinellas Plaza</a> opened at the end of June, and the drive-up lane has been wrapping around that big 25-foot cone building after dark. They're open until 10:30 every night &mdash; which makes it the perfect stop on the cart ride home from the square. I'm not saying I've been twice this week. I'm not saying I haven't.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Three new spots coming to the Market at Sawgrass Grove.</strong> <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/07/06/fmk-bringing-new-food-selections-to-market-at-sawgrass-grove/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FMK Hospitality is adding three fast-casual concepts</a>: Sizzle 'N Smash (smash burgers and milkshakes), Southern Tender (chicken tenders and fries), and Papa Joe's Pizza and More (pizza by the slice). FMK already runs Luma at the Market, so they know the room. I'll report back once the fryers are on.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Goodbye to an original.</strong> Sad news from the south side: <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/07/18/restaurant-in-the-villages-will-be-closing-its-doors/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the Fenney Grill closed its doors</a> as of Sunday, July 19. It opened back in 2017 as the very first eatery in that part of The Villages, when Fenney felt like the frontier. Nine years is a good run, and plenty of us have a sunset dinner memory from that porch. Raise a glass.</p>\n\n<p><strong>A new ER is open near Colony Plaza.</strong> File this under things you hope you never need: the new <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/07/13/opening-date-announced-for-new-adventhealth-er-on-county-road-466a/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AdventHealth freestanding ER</a> began seeing patients on July 21 &mdash; 12 patient rooms and board-certified emergency physicians, right on the 466 corridor. Put it in the back of your mind next to your other who-do-I-call notes.</p>\n\n<p>That's the week, neighbors. Music every night, ice cream until 10:30, and a new reason to visit Sawgrass Grove on the way. Pencil it in.</p>\n\n<p>See you around the square,<br>&mdash; Susan</p>"
  },
