   "title": "Your Villages Weekend + What's New: Rocky's Back on the Square",
   "date": "June 25, 2026 · By Susan Whitfield, Villages insider",
   "body": "<p>Here's the scoop, friends. The squares are humming, a fresh beach bar just opened, and the summer hours mean the music starts a little later and runs a little longer. Pour something cold and let me walk you through your weekend.</p><p>Quick note before we dance: through August, nightly music on the squares runs <strong>6 to 10 p.m.</strong>, not the old 5 to 9. Happy Hour still holds at 5 to 6. So you've got time for dinner first. I'm already planning my Saturday around it. (<a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/nightly-entertainment/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Villages Entertainment</a>)</p><h3>What to do this weekend</h3><p><strong>Friday night on the squares.</strong> Take your pick. Spanish Springs has <strong>Fancy Reagan</strong>, Lake Sumter Landing turns into a dance party with <strong>CLUB CTRL featuring DJ Lu-S</strong>, and Brownwood brings <strong>The Brothers Jukebox</strong>. All free, all 6 to 10. (<a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/nightly-entertainment/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">square schedule</a>) My tip: eat early at Lake Sumter, grab a patio table by the water, then drift toward the music. Those waterfront tables fill up fast once the band starts.</p><p><strong>Saturday is the big one.</strong> A real Villages favorite is back at Lake Sumter Landing &mdash; <strong>Rocky and The Rollers</strong>, 6 to 10. Twenty-seven years playing here and they still pack the square. Trust me on this one, get there early for a spot. Over at Spanish Springs you'll find <strong>Gravity Parade</strong>, and Brownwood has <strong>The Fire Rhythms Band</strong>. (<a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/nightly-entertainment/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">square schedule</a>)</p><p>Want a seat and air conditioning? <strong>3DN &mdash; The Ultimate 3 Dog Nite Tribute</strong> plays the Savannah Center on Saturday, 7 to 8:30 p.m. They run through all 21 of Three Dog Night's Top 40 hits &mdash; &ldquo;Joy to the World,&rdquo; &ldquo;Mama Told Me Not to Come,&rdquo; &ldquo;Shambala,&rdquo; the whole songbook. Tickets start around $35. (<a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/ticketed-performances/3dn-the-three-dog-night-experience/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">show details</a>) I sent my own neighbor to their last one and she came home singing.</p><p><strong>Sunday, ease into it.</strong> Lake Sumter Landing has <strong>The Dave Capp Project</strong>, Spanish Springs the <strong>Justin Heet Band</strong>, and Brownwood winds down with <strong>5.0.1.</strong> playing blues and soul, all 6 to 10. (<a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/nightly-entertainment/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">square schedule</a>) And if you like your evening smoother, <strong>More Jazz presents the Rick Steuart Quartet</strong> at Colony Cottage Recreation Center, starting 6 p.m. (<a href=\"https://allevents.in/the-villages/music\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">event listing</a>) A glass of wine and a little jazz on a Sunday &mdash; you're welcome.</p><p><strong>Where to eat near the music.</strong> Lake Sumter is my easy answer because you can stroll right from dinner to the band. If you're at Brownwood, do an early bite and stay for the show. And here's a happy thought for Saturday morning &mdash; the Brownwood Farmers Market runs on the square, so you can grab fresh finds before the heat sets in. (<a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/0626_PAHCalendar__BW.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Brownwood June calendar</a>)</p><h3>What's new</h3><p><strong>A new beach bar in Middleton.</strong> Say hello to <strong>Zunzibar</strong>, now open in downtown Middleton on the waterfront. It's a laid-back, beachy spot serving African, Caribbean, and Mediterranean flavors &mdash; think award-winning wings, fresh seafood, and tropical cocktails, with that big downtown water view. (<a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/06/20/new-restaurant-opening-monday-in-middleton/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Villages-News</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://mymiddleton.com/news/zunzibar-update\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Middleton</a>) I haven't been yet, so I won't oversell it &mdash; but a frozen drink by the water in June? I'll be finding out soon. Tell 'em Susan sent you.</p><p><strong>The new Walmart is open.</strong> The big <strong>Walmart on County Road 466 in Lady Lake</strong> opened its doors Wednesday, and folks were lined up early. (<a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/06/24/early-birds-out-in-force-for-opening-of-new-walmart/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Villages-News</a>) Not glamorous, I know, but a closer grocery run is a closer grocery run. Worth knowing which side of town you're on now.</p><p><strong>A second ALDI is coming.</strong> The discount grocer announced an opening date for its <strong>second Villages-area store at La Plaza Grande</strong>. (<a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/05/30/opening-date-announced-for-second-aldi-store-in-the-villages/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Villages-News</a>) If you're an ALDI quarter-for-the-cart person like me, this one's good news.</p><p>That's the honest list this week. I only put it in if I could check it, so if your favorite event isn't here, it just means I couldn't confirm the date in time &mdash; not that nothing's happening. When in doubt, I leave it out.</p><p>So that's your weekend. Music every night, a new spot to try, and Rocky and The Rollers to get you off your chair Saturday. Save me a seat by the water.</p><p>See you around the square,<br>&mdash; Susan</p>"
  },
