   "title": "Your Villages Weekend Recap: Storms, Squares & a Steakhouse on the Way",
   "date": "June 15, 2026 · By Susan Whitfield, Villages insider",
   "body": "<p>Well, friends, summer showed up and brought the heat. Here's the scoop on the weekend that just wrapped.</p><p>It was a classic June stretch — sunshine in the morning, then those low-to-mid 90s and a few afternoon thunderstorms rolling through. Saturday topped out near the mid-90s with scattered storms, and Sunday wasn't far behind. (<a href=\"https://weather.com/weather/tenday/l/The+Villages+Florida+32162?canonicalCityId=b6bc2a6e7a7c3e05c21a8b5aabf350b7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">weather.com</a>) If the music felt like it started later than usual, you weren't imagining it. The squares are on summer hours — 6 to 10 p.m. now through August 31 — to dodge the worst of the heat. Happy hour still runs 5 to 6. (<a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/lake-sumter-landing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Villages Entertainment</a>)</p><h3>Music on the squares</h3><p>Brownwood is the one I can vouch for this weekend. Saturday night, <strong>DeadLanders</strong> took the Paddock Square stage — a DeLand band that leans country, classic and southern rock. Good boot-tapping stuff. Sunday, <strong>Beauty &amp; The Beats</strong> closed things out with a '70s, '80s and '90s mix — the legends, the chart-toppers, and a few one-hit wonders you forgot you loved. (<a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/brownwood/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Brownwood lineup</a>)</p><p>A little Susan honesty: the nightly calendars roll forward fast, so by Monday the Friday and Saturday names at Lake Sumter Landing and Spanish Springs had already cycled off the public page. Rather than guess, I'll point you to the live lineups so you can plan the week ahead — both <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/lake-sumter-landing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Lake Sumter Landing</a> and <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/brownwood/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Brownwood</a> keep theirs updated. Easiest way to never miss your favorite band.</p><h3>A sip worth knowing</h3><p>Heading to the bar huts this month? The June feature is a <strong>Tequila Sunrise</strong> — $8 single, $10.50 double, while supplies last. Pretty in the cup and easy on a warm night. (<a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/bar-huts/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">bar huts</a>) I sent my own neighbor for one Saturday. She approved.</p><h3>On the dining radar</h3><p>One for the foodies. A new spot is on the horizon at the Woodlands Championship Golf Course: <strong>Luxe Steakhouse &amp; Cellar</strong>, announced back in late March. It's the latest from Jack Suleiman, the same name behind RedSauce over at Lake Sumter Landing — so the bar's set high. No opening date yet (they say watch your Vmail), but steaks with a view of the greens? I'll be there. (<a href=\"https://www.thevillages.com/whats-new/shopping-dining/luxe-steakhouse-cellar-coming-soon/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Villages — Shopping &amp; Dining</a>)</p><h3>Who-knew note</h3><p>Saturday-morning treasure hunters had a good one. There was a neighborhood garage sale Friday and Saturday over in the <strong>Village of Calumet Grove</strong>, on SE 171st Horseshoe Lane, 7:30 to 12:30. (<a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Villages-News.com</a>) The early birds always get the good stuff — that's just the law of the land here. Watch the Villages-News listings and the Daily Sun calendar if you like a good Saturday rummage.</p><h3>The bottom line</h3><p>Quieter, hotter weekend on the squares — the kind where you sip something cold, catch a band after the sun drops, and let the storms pass. I kept this one to what I could actually confirm, because I'd rather tell you the truth than fill the page. There's a steakhouse coming, the music plays every night, and summer's just getting started.</p><p>Now go enjoy yourself.</p><p>See you around the square,<br>— Susan</p>"
